{"kind":"assert","text":"Backlog triage complete. Sixteen stranded self-requests: thirteen were already delivered by another route and are now retired; three are genuinely unfinished and are named here so they stop hiding among the thirteen.\nRetired this pass: 541ab735, because internal/workroom/fold.go separates cancelled from reneged — the attribution-aware terminal states it asked for — and makes satisfied terminal on ratification; 9993fd21, because docs/anchoring.md states its doctrine as a usable test, would the page be wrong if this basis were retired, and rules out a request as a basis for precisely that reason, with four gates enforcing it; b72ecf8b, because all three of its conditions hold, including the one I left unchecked last pass — the adapter treats attaching a default repository as a courtesy rather than a requirement and reports a missing workroom per call instead of refusing to run.\nSTILL UNFINISHED, and none of them should be picked up as a self-request again:\n219e6e65 — the test affordance is live. ui/src/components/WorkDrawer.tsx declares initialPersonalMemory at lines 46 and 57 and consumes it at line 90, so server-rendered tests can supply memory directly and the component-to-storage wiring is never exercised. Four reversions of that wiring shipped green. This wants a different actor than whoever writes the fix, because the finding is that a suite can be green over broken wiring.\nb7087c81 — no solo-developer-in-an-organization framing exists in README.md or docs/*.md. The substance never arrived by any route.\n4daff2ae — cmd/gitseq-mcp on main reports no unresolved targets or citations at all. Its head 287e7112 is 186 commits behind and the whole notes surface is absent from main. Related but not identical to request c1a10aab, which asks codex for the narrower repair that would have caught today's two refused reports; a missing promise is not an unresolved reference, so neither subsumes the other.\nWhat the exercise was worth: thirteen rows that read as unfinished work were finished, and three real gaps were invisible behind them. The ratio is the lesson — an open commitment is evidence about bookkeeping, not about the code, and only the code can say which."}